@startuml
title 3.16.14 Assign or remove campaign items
caption UC-161 | Planned | Proposed design
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: docs/requirements/uc.md
' Main entity migration: No migration: proposed entity only
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Staff / Admin" as Actor
participant "Donation Campaign UI (proposed)" as Page
participant "Campaign API (proposed)" as API
participant "Campaign Service (proposed)" as Service
participant "donation_campaigns" as Table <<proposed entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Assign or remove campaign items
activate Page
Page -> Page: 2: Select campaign, items and add/remove action
Page -> API: 3: Assign or remove campaign items (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 4: Proposed: authenticate active session and authorize STAFF or ADMIN
alt Session and required permission are valid
    API -> API: 5: Proposed: validate ids and item-management permission
    alt Request input is valid
        API -> Service: 6: Assign or remove campaign items for the current actor
        activate Service
        Service -> Service: 7: Begin proposed transaction
        Service -> Table: 8: Lock campaign and verify editable processing state (proposed)
        activate Table
        Table --> Service: 9: Campaign state
        deactivate Table
        Service -> Service: 10: Lock selected custody items; inspect retention, claims,\nappointments, disputes, holds and processing state
        alt Campaign is editable and selected items are eligible/unprocessed
            Service -> Service: 11: Add eligible membership or remove unprocessed membership; keep prior\nitem outcomes
            Service -> Table: 12: Record campaign membership revision (proposed)
            activate Table
            Table --> Service: 13: Proposed updated campaign revision
            deactivate Table
            Service -> Service: 14: Record membership history and actor; commit
            Service --> API: 15: Updated campaign membership (proposed)
            API --> Page: 16: HTTP 200 (proposed): Updated campaign membership (proposed)
            Page --> Actor: 17: Display assigned items; do not execute disposition
        else Campaign closed, item blocked or already processed
            Service --> API: 11.1: Membership change is not allowed
            API --> Page: 11.2: HTTP 409 (proposed)
            Page --> Actor: 11.3: Display error; do not report success
        end
        deactivate Service
    else Invalid request input
        API --> Page: 6.1: Proposed validation error response
        Page --> Actor: 6.2: Display validation errors; do not execute the operation
    end
else Missing/invalid session or required permission
    API --> Page: 5.1: Proposed authentication/access error response
    Page --> Actor: 5.2: Show session or access error; no protected result
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend bottom left
PLANNED: campaign and membership schema/API/UI are absent. donation_campaigns is the proposed main
entity; membership is abstracted inside the service.
endlegend

@enduml
